    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first creates a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows without dropping tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder takes the low-resolution image and produces the dense feature field. That feature field is the carrier that persists through the method. The window partition operates on the feature field and keeps every token in the next representation.",
